    {"source_id":"D166-GATECH-NS-VIMPC-SOFTWARE","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"Georgia Institute of Technology, Dynamics and Control Systems Laboratory","title":"NS-VIMPC: Sampling-Based MPC with Neural Control Barrier Functions","url":"https://dcsl.gatech.edu/software/nsvimpc/","source_family":"university lab software / research implementation","locator":"Official lab page inspected 2026-10-26. Describes Python implementation pairing sampling-based MPC with a neural control barrier function for safety beyond the MPC horizon; reproduces simulations for AutoRally, planar quadrotor and Dubins car; includes training/evaluation scripts and offline data collection; names JAX/PyTorch and MIT license; links to RSS 2025 and RA-L 2023 papers.","supports":"A concrete research software example connecting MPPI-style sampling control, learned safety barriers, simulation and reproducible code; useful for evaluating how learned safety components complement rather than replace model-based control.","claim_limit":"Research software validated in listed simulation settings, not road-vehicle deployment or certification. The page's safety terminology does not establish an unconditional guarantee for a target AV; assumptions and paper-specific theorem conditions must be inspected before reuse.","search_status":"official university lab software page inspected 2026-10-26","credibility_assessment":"Primary lab-maintained project page with linked publications, implementation language, license and test scope. Credible for repository description; performance/safety claims remain bounded to the underlying papers and simulated platforms."},
