    {"source_id":"D011-CFA-CONTINGENT-CLAIMS-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"CFA Institute","title":"Valuation of Contingent Claims (2026 Level II Derivatives)","url":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/valuation-contingent-claims","source_family":"professional curriculum / pricing methods","locator":"2026 derivatives reading: contingent claims/options, model-based valuation and no-arbitrage links; forward/futures/swaps addressed in related curriculum.","supports":"Financial engineering/pricing work and instrument-specific valuation context.","claim_limit":"Curriculum outcome is not a complete catalogue of production pricing models, calibration workflows or model validation requirements.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-GARP-FRM-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Global Association of Risk Professionals","title":"FRM Program and Exam Topics","url":"https://www.garp.org/frm/program-exams","source_family":"professional body / credential syllabus","locator":"FRM topic areas and current exam coverage for quantitative analysis, financial markets/products, valuation/risk models and applied risk areas.","supports":"Professional risk knowledge families and terminology.","claim_limit":"Credential syllabus, not proof that FRM is required, that all finance roles are risk roles, or that its topic list exhausts the domain.","search_status":"existing_area_source_capture_requires_current_page_reopen"},
    {"source_id":"D011-ONET-QFA-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"U.S. Department of Labor, O*NET Resource Center","title":"Financial Quantitative Analysts, 13-2099.01","url":"https://www.onetonline.org/link/details/13-2099.01","source_family":"official occupational task/skill dataset","locator":"Tasks, detailed work activities, worker requirements/software skills. Core tasks include applying math/statistics to derivative valuation, trading and risk; developing portfolio/pricing tools and models; interpreting analyses; model verification; testing analytical software.","supports":"Quant analyst/researcher/developer task cluster and technical work outputs.","claim_limit":"US occupation survey/profile and broad SOC category; overlaps several titles and does not prove an individual D011 role identity or a universal tool requirement. Software demand page is US postings data for 2025.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-CFA-TCA-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"CFA Institute","title":"Trading Costs and Electronic Markets (2026)" ,"url":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/trading-costs-and-electronic-markets","source_family":"professional curriculum / market microstructure and trading costs","locator":"Current 2026 learning outcomes and summary: explicit and implicit costs; effective spreads and VWAP transaction-cost estimates; implementation shortfall; electronic trading systems, algorithms and risks.","supports":"Separates post-trade cost measurement (implementation shortfall/VWAP) from the execution policy itself and describes the market-impact, delay and opportunity-cost components that execution methods manage.","claim_limit":"Professional curriculum explains standard concepts; it does not establish one universally best benchmark, execution algorithm, asset-class practice or learner prerequisite sequence.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-BIS-FX-EXECUTION-ALGORITHMS-2020","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Bank for International Settlements, Markets Committee","title":"FX Execution Algorithms and Market Functioning","url":"https://www.bis.org/publications/fx-execution-algorithms-and-market-functioning","source_family":"intergovernmental market-practice report / credible grey literature","locator":"Markets Committee paper 13, published 2020-10-30; report overview and sections on execution-algorithm types, user/provider survey, FX market structure, execution and operational risks.","supports":"In FX, passive/pegged, sweeping/limit-based, implementation-shortfall, TWAP/VWAP and participation algorithms expose different market-impact, market-risk, completion and opportunity-cost trade-offs; hybrid algorithms may switch with conditions.","claim_limit":"A 2020 FX-focused survey/report, not a current universal algorithm taxonomy, proof of causal market effects or evidence that FX findings transfer unchanged to equities, derivatives or every venue. Publisher outreach and market scope are stated; corroborate empirical claims.","search_status":"opened_and_inspected_2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-BERTIMAS-LO-EXECUTION-1998","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Elsevier, Journal of Financial Markets","title":"Optimal Control of Execution Costs","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1386418197000128","source_family":"peer-reviewed market-microstructure/optimal-execution research","locator":"Bertsimas and Lo (1998), Journal of Financial Markets 1(1), pp. 1Ã¢â‚¬â€œ50; publisher record/abstract inspected 2026-10-23.","supports":"Foundational dynamic optimization formulation for splitting a large order across a fixed horizon to minimize expected execution costs under a specified price-impact function; extends to portfolios and constraints.","claim_limit":"The article's price dynamics, impact specification, horizon and assumptions define a model family, not a universal production schedule or evidence that its optimal policy remains optimal under different order books, information, fees or regulatory constraints.","search_status":"publisher record and abstract opened 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-ALMGREN-CHRISS-EXECUTION-2001","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Incisive Media / Journal of Risk","title":"Optimal Execution of Portfolio Transactions","url":"https://doi.org/10.21314/JOR.2001.041","source_family":"peer-reviewed quantitative finance / optimal-execution research","locator":"Almgren and Chriss, Journal of Risk 3 (2001); publisher record/abstract inspected 2026-10-23.","supports":"Extends expected-cost execution with variance risk and permanent/temporary market-impact costs, yielding a cost-risk frontier for portfolio liquidation and a model-based choice of urgency/risk tolerance.","claim_limit":"Linear market-impact and price-risk assumptions are a tractable benchmark. Calibration, nonlinear/transient impact, limit-order fills, alpha, venue rules, capacity and current out-of-sample validation require additional models/evidence.","search_status":"publisher record and abstract opened 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-CARTEA-JAIMUNGAL-EXECUTION-ORDERS-2015","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Taylor & Francis, Quantitative Finance","title":"Optimal Execution with Limit and Market Orders","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/14697688.2015.1032543","source_family":"peer-reviewed quantitative finance / limit-order execution research","locator":"Cartea and Jaimungal, Quantitative Finance 15(8), pp. 1279Ã¢â‚¬â€œ1291 (2015); publisher record/abstract inspected 2026-10-23.","supports":"Adds a discrete order-choice branch to optimal scheduling: selecting and constraining market versus limit orders and limit depth, with inventory schedule and fill/execution uncertainty in the policy.","claim_limit":"Model-based paper and bounded market setting; not evidence that limit orders dominate market orders generally or that results transfer across liquidity regimes, venues, products and current market rules.","search_status":"publisher record and abstract opened 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-IJCAI-GENERALIZABLE-RL-EXECUTION-2023","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence","title":"Towards Generalizable Reinforcement Learning for Trade Execution","url":"https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2023/553","source_family":"peer-reviewed AI/finance conference research","locator":"IJCAI 2023 Main Track, pp. 4975Ã¢â‚¬â€œ4983; official proceedings page and abstract inspected 2026-10-23.","supports":"An emerging offline-RL execution approach learns from historical order-book context in simulation; its explicit focus on context representation and overfitting indicates that a learned policy must be evaluated for generalization, not just in-simulator reward.","claim_limit":"Research proposes methods and reports results in its simulator/benchmark; it does not establish real-market deployment, robust profitability or universal superiority over classical execution baselines.","search_status":"official proceedings paper opened 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-CHEN-LUDOVSKI-VOSS-ML-EXECUTION-SURROGATES-2023","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Taylor & Francis, Quantitative Finance","title":"On Parametric Optimal Execution and Machine Learning Surrogates","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/14697688.2023.2282657","source_family":"peer-reviewed quantitative finance / machine-learning method research","locator":"Chen, Ludkovski and VoÃƒÅ¸, Quantitative Finance 24(1) (2024 issue; published online 2023); publisher record/abstract inspected 2026-10-23.","supports":"Combines a dynamic-programming baseline with deep actor-critic neural surrogates for nonlinear transient market impact and multiple market/model parameters; links learned function approximation to classical stochastic-control execution objectives.","claim_limit":"The method is evaluated on stated parameterized models and reproducible notebook; market-impact calibration is difficult and model/simulator assumptions constrain conclusions. It does not make deep RL a default or remove the need for classical baselines and sensitivity checks.","search_status":"journal record/abstract inspected 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-WANG-GAO-LI-RL-EXECUTION-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Springer Nature, Finance and Stochastics","title":"Reinforcement Learning for Continuous-Time Optimal Execution: Actor-Critic Algorithm and Error Analysis","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00780-026-00589-5","source_family":"peer-reviewed quantitative finance / current machine-learning research","locator":"Open-access Finance and Stochastics 30 (2026), pp. 597Ã¢â‚¬â€œ655; published 2026-03-10; article inspected 2026-10-23.","supports":"A current research example that derives RL policy/value parameterization from the analytical AlmgrenÃ¢â‚¬â€œChriss objective, adds an actor-critic recalibration step and finite-time convergence analysis, and compares with classical and deep-RL methods using historical-order-flow and simulated limit-order-book environments.","claim_limit":"The convergence guarantee is conditional on the paper's assumptions/learning rates and the empirical comparisons use bounded data/simulators; authors explicitly identify out-of-distribution and model-misspecification concerns. It is not proof of live-market superiority or a production-ready execution tool.","search_status":"official Springer open-access article inspected 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-BIRMINGHAM-FINANCIAL-ECONOMETRICS-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"University of Birmingham, Birmingham Business School","title":"LM Financial Econometrics (2026/27 module description)","url":"https://program-and-modules-handbook.bham.ac.uk/webhandbooks/WebHandbooks-control-servlet?Action=getModuleDetailsList&pgCrse=36331&pgSubj=07&searchTerm=002026","source_family":"official university financial-econometrics curriculum","locator":"Official module search result for 2026/27 LM Financial Econometrics; direct page reopen returned 502. Description lists multivariate regression, MLE/moments/GMM, misspecification, measurement error/IV, DiD, RDD, financial time series/volatility, panel regression, event studies and qualitative-response models.","supports":"A finance-specific curriculum cross-check that treats financial econometrics as several methods chosen by data structure and question, not a single technique; shows both predictive/time-series and identification/empirical-design branches.","claim_limit":"One master's module and official search-result description, not a global consensus, proof all listed methods are compulsory, or universal prerequisite graph.","search_status":"official course search result inspected 2026-10-23; direct reopen 502"},
    {"source_id":"D011-YORK-FINANCIAL-ECONOMETRICS-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"University of York","title":"Financial Econometrics (ECO00084M), 2026/27","url":"https://www.york.ac.uk/students/studying/manage/programmes/module-catalogue/module/ECO00084M/2026-27?creditLevel=&department=&electiveTheme=&isAvailableAsElective=false&isAvailableToVisitingStudents=true&max=15&offset=180&query=&teachingPeriod=","source_family":"official university financial-econometrics curriculum","locator":"Official 2026/27 module-catalogue search result; direct URL reopen returned a cache miss. Outcomes and content list regression assumptions, OLS/MLE/GMM, endogeneity, ARMA, unit roots/spurious regression, VAR/Granger/cointegration, GARCH, factor models, quantile/VaR and switching models.","supports":"Another finance-specific curriculum cross-check linking estimation/inference foundations to cross-section, time-series, volatility, asset-pricing and risk-model branches; emphasizes assumptions and technique selection for financial data.","claim_limit":"One university module and course description; establishes its instructional scope only, not universal use or exact role/route requirements. Software choice EViews is program-specific.","search_status":"official course result inspected 2026-10-23; direct reopen cache miss"},
    {"source_id":"D011-NHH-FINANCIAL-ECONOMETRICS-2026","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"NHH Norwegian School of Economics","title":"FIN538 Financial Econometrics (Autumn 2026)","url":"https://www.nhh.no/en/courses/financial-econometrics2/","source_family":"official university financial-econometrics curriculum","locator":"Official course page opened 2026-10-23; topics at lines 21Ã¢â‚¬â€œ45; learning outcomes and access/prerequisites at lines 46Ã¢â‚¬â€œ79. Page is for Autumn 2026, though its overview also displays an offering-status inconsistency; preserve the content/date and do not infer current enrollment availability.","supports":"Broad, explicit finance-method map covering OLS/MLE/GMM; panel/fixed-effects and time-series/volatility; causal designs IV/RDD/DiD/randomized/selection-on-observables; event studies, BHAR/CTAR, matching and Fama-MacBeth.","claim_limit":"Restricted advanced course with stated econometrics/asset-pricing prerequisites; course inclusion does not make every method compulsory for all roles or determine a fixed learner sequence.","search_status":"official course page opened 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-LINEARMODELS-7-1","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"linearmodels open-source project","title":"linearmodels 7.1: Panel, Instrumental-Variable and Asset-Pricing Model Documentation","url":"https://bashtage.github.io/linearmodels/","source_family":"maintained open-source statistical/econometric software documentation / credible grey implementation evidence","locator":"Version 7.1 docs opened 2026-10-23; documents fixed/random/first-difference/between/pooled/Fama-MacBeth panel estimators, IV2SLS, LIML, IV-GMM/CUE/JIVE, linear factor model/SUR estimators and weak-identification, exogeneity, overidentification and panel-specification tests.","supports":"Concrete implementation map showing estimator alternatives and diagnostics for distinct panel, endogenous-regressor, GMM and empirical-asset-pricing tasks; clarifies that estimator choice entails identifying assumptions and specification checks.","claim_limit":"Maintainer documentation reports software scope and implementation, not unbiased results for a dataset, a complete methods textbook, universal preference, or proof of model assumptions. Verify theory, versions, data structure and inference design separately.","search_status":"maintained official documentation inspected 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-FAMA-MACBETH-1973","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"University of Chicago Press, Journal of Political Economy","title":"Risk, Return, and Equilibrium: Empirical Tests","url":"https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/10.1086/260061","source_family":"peer-reviewed asset-pricing methodology / foundational empirical research","locator":"Fama and MacBeth (1973), Journal of Political Economy 81(3), pp. 607Ã¢â‚¬â€œ636; publisher record and abstract inspected 2026-10-23. Full text is subscriber-gated.","supports":"Foundational two-pass empirical test of the relationship between average stock returns and risk, providing context for the later named Fama-MacBeth cross-sectional estimation procedure in asset-pricing research.","claim_limit":"Historical US-equity study of specific equilibrium hypotheses; citation does not establish that the estimator is suitable for every panel, asset-pricing question, market or current model.","search_status":"publisher record/abstract opened 2026-10-23; full text gated"},
    {"source_id":"D011-CHERNOZHUKOV-DML-2018","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Oxford University Press, The Econometrics Journal","title":"Double/Debiased Machine Learning for Treatment and Structural Parameters","url":"https://academic.oup.com/ectj/article/21/1/C1/5056401?login=false","source_family":"peer-reviewed econometric methods research","locator":"Chernozhukov et al. (2018), The Econometrics Journal 21(1), C1Ã¢â‚¬â€œC68; Oxford Academic article record/summary inspected 2026-10-23.","supports":"A principled bridge from modern ML to econometric inference: flexible learners estimate high-dimensional nuisance functions, while Neyman-orthogonal scores and cross-fitting target low-dimensional causal/structural parameters under stated conditions.","claim_limit":"DML does not create identification where assumptions fail; validity depends on the estimand, design, score, dependence structure, nuisance convergence and implementation. Ordinary supervised prediction, feature importance or black-box accuracy is not itself causal inference.","search_status":"publisher record and abstract inspected 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D011-ELGHOUL-INTERNATIONAL-EVENT-STUDY-2022","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Springer Nature / Journal of International Business Studies; indexed by PubMed","title":"Event Studies in International Finance Research","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35822194/","source_family":"peer-reviewed international-finance methods review","locator":"El Ghoul, Guedhami, Mansi and Sy (2022), Journal of International Business Studies 53(2), pp. 344Ã¢â‚¬â€œ364; PubMed record and indexed article abstract inspected 2026-10-23. Full text linked via PMC but direct fetch was bot-blocked.","supports":"Reviews event selection, event/estimation windows, normal-return models, abnormal-return inference and short- versus long-horizon challenges in cross-country equity and fixed-income research; emphasizes model and international-market heterogeneity.","claim_limit":"A literature review with recommendations, not a universal event-study protocol or causal identification guarantee. Long-horizon abnormal-return conclusions remain especially sensitive to expected-return model and market regime.","search_status":"official PubMed bibliographic/abstract record inspected 2026-10-23; PMC full text direct fetch blocked"},
