    {"source_id":"D166-LANELET2-MAP-FRAMEWORK","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"FZI Research Center for Information Technology / Lanelet2 project","title":"Lanelet2: Map Handling Framework for Automated Driving","url":"https://github.com/fzi-forschungszentrum-informatik/Lanelet2","source_family":"maintained open-source project technical documentation / credible grey literature","locator":"Project README and linked docs describe a 2D/3D HD-map handling library with traffic-rule-aware lanelets, participant-specific routing, lane changes/areas, coordinate projection, OSM-based read/write, map creation/modification tools and map validation; maps encode boundaries, centerlines and regulatory elements.","supports":"Primary implementation context for HD road-network representation, map authoring/editing, topology, traffic-rule interpretation, routing and validation; clarifies that map data feed localization/planning rather than constituting a generic raster basemap.","claim_limit":"A particular open-source map framework, not an industry-wide standard or complete map-production workflow. Do not confuse Lanelet2's OSM serialization with ordinary OSM maps being AV-ready; project support and format choices are implementation-specific.","credibility_assessment":"Credible first-party project evidence: maintained source repository, inspectable implementation/docs and explicit license. It establishes Lanelet2 capabilities and design only; independent research and other specifications are needed for prevalence, map correctness and safety claims.","search_status":"project README, architecture/primitive docs and map-editor instructions opened and inspected 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D166-ASRAT-CHO-HD-MAP-SURVEY-2024","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"ISPRS International Journal of Geo-Information","title":"A Comprehensive Survey on High-Definition Map Generation and Maintenance","url":"https://www.mdpi.com/2220-9964/13/7/232","source_family":"peer-reviewed survey / academic literature","locator":"2024 open-access survey reviews HD-map creation, updates, sensor fusion, point-cloud generation, SLAM and open research challenges; search-indexed article text reports no single adopted HD-map structure across industry. Direct page retrieval returned HTTP 429 during this pass, so the abstract/indexed content, bibliographic metadata and DOI were inspected; full methods/references were not reread.","supports":"Independent research map for traditional HD-map production and maintenance tasks, emerging update pipelines, format fragmentation and open research questions; use it to widen the subsequent leaf-level map-method search.","claim_limit":"Survey-level synthesis, not a standard or proof of the maturity/prevalence of any one commercial workflow. Direct full-text inspection was blocked in this pass; do not rely on uninspected details or treat the reported lack of a unified structure as a normative claim.","credibility_assessment":"Peer-reviewed journal survey with named authors, date, DOI and explicit scope; credible as a research synthesis, subject to journal/editorial quality checks and the current access limitation. Verify cited primary studies before using particular techniques or industry claims.","search_status":"bibliographic record and indexed abstract inspected 2026-10-23; direct fetch rate-limited HTTP 429; full-text review open"},
    {"source_id":"D166-TSUSHIMA-ETAL-HD-MAP-PRODUCTION-2020","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"ISPRS Archives / International Society for Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing","title":"Creation of High Definition Map for Autonomous Driving","url":"https://isprs-archives.copernicus.org/articles/XLIII-B4-2020/415/2020/","source_family":"peer-reviewed conference paper / photogrammetry and remote-sensing literature","locator":"Open paper describes a five-step production line: mobile-mapping-system survey, 3D plotting, feature-attribute editing and road-network topology construction, format conversion, and quality assurance; it reports practical production experience and discusses the lack of a settled open HD-map production standard at publication time.","supports":"Concrete production-task breakdown for HD-map surveying, geometric/semantic editing, topology, conversion and QA; complements Lanelet2's representation/tooling and ASAM OpenDRIVE's simulation format scope.","claim_limit":"2020 project/production account rather than a universal or current workflow; one production setting and paper date limit generalization. Cross-check modern crowdsourced/online map-update methods and current specifications.","credibility_assessment":"Traceable scholarly paper in the ISPRS Archives with DOI, named authors and inspectable open text; useful for a documented production workflow, not a current industry consensus or independent validation of all map providers.","search_status":"full ISPRS article page and abstract opened 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D166-AUTOSAR-ADAPTIVE-PLATFORM-R25-11","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"AUTOSAR","title":"AUTOSAR Adaptive Platform (R25-11)","url":"https://www.autosar.org/standards/adaptive-platform","source_family":"automotive industry standard / platform architecture","locator":"Current release R25-11; official overview describes runtime services and standardized interfaces, service-oriented communication, Classic/Adaptive coexistence and signal-to-service translation, diagnostics, networking, time synchronization, health management, sensor interfaces, update/configuration management and redundant/fail-operational design goals for high-performance automotive compute.","supports":"System-integration architecture context for connecting autonomous-driving applications with mixed legacy ECUs and high-performance compute, coordinating services, diagnostics, updates and vehicle/network interfaces.","claim_limit":"AUTOSAR defines standardized platform interfaces and behavior, not a complete AV stack or proof every vehicle uses AUTOSAR Adaptive. Detailed specs and commercial exploitation are license/IPR constrained; marketing claims such as fail-operational capability must be tied to a particular compliant implementation and safety evidence.","credibility_assessment":"Primary source from the standards organization for its current release and stated scope. The overview is not a substitute for applicable specifications, OEM architecture evidence or system safety validation; implementation remains platform- and vehicle-specific.","search_status":"official AUTOSAR overview and R25-11 release sections inspected 2026-10-23"},
    {"source_id":"D166-ASAM-SOVD-1-0-0","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"ASAM","title":"ASAM Service-Oriented Vehicle Diagnostics (SOVD) 1.0.0","url":"https://www.asam.net/standards/detail/sovd/","source_family":"automotive standards body / technical standard","locator":"Current published standard page lists v1.0.0 (2022-06-30), API/OpenAPI scope and diagnostic communication to HPCs/ECUs, software updates, logging and data transfer. ASAM describes SOVD as REST/JSON/OAuth API-based and explicitly states it is intended to coexist with UDS, extending diagnostics for dynamic software/HPC systems rather than replacing established UDS use.","supports":"Modern software-defined-vehicle diagnostic and integration context: access distributed application/HPC diagnostics, logging, software-update and data interfaces across remote, proximity and in-vehicle scenarios.","claim_limit":"SOVD specifies an API, not the in-vehicle implementation, complete vehicle integration architecture or safety evidence. v1.0.0 is published while v1.2.0 is under development toward a planned 2028 release; verify current version and applicable ISO adoption before relying on it.","credibility_assessment":"Primary standards-body source with version/date, scope and authoring-participant information; strong for what ASAM SOVD specifies and its intended relation to UDS. It does not establish market adoption, implementation quality or universal role requirements.","search_status":"official ASAM datasheet and standard scope opened and inspected 2026-10-23; active 1.2.0 development checked"},
    {"source_id":"D166-ISO-14229-1-2026-UDS","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"International Organization for Standardization (ISO)","title":"ISO 14229-1:2026: Unified Diagnostic Services (UDS), Application Layer","url":"https://committee.iso.org/standard/87962.html?browse=tc","source_family":"international automotive standard","locator":"Published fourth edition, June 2026; abstract specifies client/server diagnostic services for in-vehicle ECUs, including vehicle/sensor data access, diagnostic information, actuator control and routine control. The standard is data-link independent and explicitly does not specify implementation requirements; full standard is paid.","supports":"Current ECU-centric diagnostic fundamentals for investigating vehicle subsystems and reading/clearing fault or sensor data; provides the established protocol baseline against which SOVD's software/HPC diagnostic extension is contextualized.","claim_limit":"Standard describes diagnostic services, not the diagnostic system implementation, autonomous-driving architecture, or a complete vehicle communication protocol. It does not prove that any particular D166 role performs diagnostics; applicability depends on vehicle/OEM network and assigned duties.","credibility_assessment":"Primary international standard page with publication status, edition/date and abstract. Only its public abstract was reviewed; full requirements are paywalled, so avoid claims beyond that scope.","search_status":"official ISO standard record/abstract inspected 2026-10-23; full text paid"},
    {"source_id":"D166-ASAM-OSI-SIMULATION-INTERFACES-3-8","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"ASAM","title":"ASAM Open Simulation Interface (OSI), Version 3.8.0","url":"https://opensimulationinterface.github.io/osi-antora-generator/asamosi/latest/specification/index.html","source_family":"automotive simulation standard / open technical specification","locator":"Current official documentation identifies OSI 3.8.0 as a specification for interfaces among distributed simulation models, especially environmental perception for automated-driving functions; it defines generic messages/interfaces such as GroundTruth, SensorData, SensorView and FeatureData to support modular/interoperable simulator components.","supports":"Simulation-side system-integration and verification context: standardizes data exchange among environment, sensor, perception and function models so simulation components can be connected and tested across implementations.","claim_limit":"OSI is a simulation interface, not the production vehicle's sensor bus or vehicle-command interface, not a map format and not a safety-validation argument by itself. Version-specific interfaces and licensing must be checked for the selected simulator/tool chain.","credibility_assessment":"Primary ASAM specification with public versioned documentation and explicit interface scope; appropriate for simulator interoperability claims, not for general production-vehicle integration prevalence.","search_status":"official ASAM OSI documentation/version inspected 2026-10-23; previous docs URL redirects to current specification path"},
