    {"source_id":"D166-AUTOWARE-TRAJECTORY-FOLLOWER-CONTROL","domain_id":"D166","publisher":"Autoware Foundation","title":"Autoware Trajectory Follower Nodes","url":"https://autowarefoundation.github.io/autoware_universe/main/control/autoware_trajectory_follower_node/","source_family":"maintained open-source AV software documentation / credible grey literature","locator":"Current Universe docs inspected 2026-10-23; reference trajectory, odometry and steering status feed a follower; it emits combined lateral/longitudinal commands, checks timeouts, offers lateral MPC or Pure Pursuit, and currently uses longitudinal PID in this node.","supports":"Concrete mapping from planner trajectory and vehicle state to steering/speed/acceleration commands, plus one maintained implementation showing separate lateral/longitudinal control modules and selectable controller implementations.","claim_limit":"Autoware-specific current implementation, not a universal stack or evidence every AV uses MPC/Pure Pursuit/PID. Controller needs depend on vehicle model, interface, operating envelope and validation.","credibility_assessment":"High credibility for the maintained Autoware implementation and its documented interfaces because the project documentation is directly accessible and linked to maintained code. It is project-specific and cannot establish field prevalence, comparative performance or safety.","search_status":"official project documentation opened and inspected 2026-10-23"},
