VERIFIED_THIS_PASS.update({
    "https://docs.autoware.org/main/design/autoware-architecture-v1/interfaces/components/localization/": "Opened current Autoware localization interface documentation 2026-10-23. It specifies point-cloud map/LiDAR NDT inputs, manual or INS-derived initialization, GNSS position/orientation inputs, and localization interfaces. Supports a concrete configured component contract, not a universal AV architecture.",
    "https://docs.autoware.org/main/tutorials/integrating-autoware/launch-autoware/localization/": "Opened current Autoware localization launch tutorial 2026-10-23. It documents NDT, camera-based YabLoc, GNSS/IMU/wheel-odometry Eagleye, and twist-source configuration, plus configuration/diagnostic caveats. These are implementation choices dependent on the vehicle, map and sensors.",
    "https://autowarefoundation.github.io/autoware_core/pr-248/localization/autoware_ekf_localizer/": "Inspected Autoware EKF localizer documentation 2026-10-23. The package fuses ego-pose and ego-twist with a 2D vehicle model, delay compensation, yaw-bias estimation, Mahalanobis outlier gating, smoothing, covariance and diagnostics. It is a project-specific local pose/twist estimator, not a general multi-sensor INS stack.",
    "https://autowarefoundation.github.io/autoware.universe_planning/pr-5583/localization/ndt_scan_matcher/": "Inspected Autoware NDT scan matcher documentation 2026-10-23. It matches LiDAR scans against a point-cloud map from an initial pose and emits pose/covariance/diagnostics; documents Monte Carlo initialization, score/time monitoring and timeouts. Repository-version-specific implementation evidence.",
    "https://autowarefoundation.github.io/autoware_universe/latest/localization/autoware_pose_covariance_modifier/": "Inspected Autoware pose-covariance modifier documentation 2026-10-23. It combines/selects GNSS and NDT pose/covariance under map, GNSS-quality and extrinsic-calibration assumptions; documents fixed/unreliable NDT covariance and that this package is disabled by default. This limitation must accompany any uncertainty claim.",
    "https://autowarefoundation.github.io/autoware_universe/latest/localization/autoware_pose_estimator_arbiter/": "Inspected Autoware pose-estimator arbiter documentation 2026-10-23. It names NDT, Eagleye, YabLoc and landmark estimators and currently documents a limited switching rule/demo. Evidence for configurable implementation options, not proof of robust general-purpose failover.",
    "https://github.com/ApolloAuto/apollo/blob/master/modules/localization/msf/README.md?plain=1": "Inspected current Apollo MSF README 2026-10-23. Describes GNSS, LiDAR and IMU/SINS, maps, four GNSS-use modes, LiDAR intensity/altitude/fusion variants, confidence/status output, data/configuration requirements and x86_64 platform limit. First-party implementation documentation, not a field-wide requirement.",
    "https://github.com/ApolloAuto/apollo/blob/master/docs/05_Localization/how_to_run_MSF_localization_module_on_your_local_computer.md": "Inspected Apollo MSF run guide 2026-10-23. It documents map and extrinsic/lever-arm setup, execution/replay and evaluation. Specific workflow evidence; does not prove every localization system has the same map or setup requirements.",
    "https://gtsam.org/docs/": "Opened current GTSAM documentation 2026-10-23 (4.3 documentation). GTSAM is a factor-graph library for robotics/computer vision with IMU preintegration and Python/MATLAB interfaces. Supports estimator implementation context, not a localization algorithm by itself.",
    "https://gtsam.org/tutorials/intro.html": "Inspected GTSAM introductory factor-graph tutorial 2026-10-23. It explains variables and measurement constraints and their use in SLAM/SfM. General estimation foundation; not AV-specific evidence.",
    "https://github.com/TixiaoShan/LIO-SAM": "Inspected the maintained LIO-SAM project README 2026-10-23. It documents LiDAR-inertial smoothing/mapping, optional GPS factors, loop closure/ICP, high-rate IMU and extrinsic-transform requirements, and sensor-specific limitations. Research implementation example, not a universal AV stack.",
    "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11370-024-00515-8": "Opened the 2024 peer-reviewed open LiDAR odometry survey 2026-10-23. It organizes wheel, IMU, camera, radar and LiDAR odometry, including LiDAR-only, LiDAR-IMU and multi-sensor families, datasets and evaluation. Survey taxonomy only; verify primary-study performance claims.",
    "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41315-026-00528-9": "Opened the full open 2026 robotics localization survey (published 2026-03-30) 2026-10-23. It surveys estimator algorithms, map references and sensor modalities, including global/relative, semantic and learned approaches; learning generally augments components in surveyed examples. Broad robotics scope, not exclusively road AVs; do not infer a universal method ladder.",
    "https://www.mdpi.com/2075-1702/12/2/118": "Indexed the bibliographic page/abstract for the 2024 peer-reviewed self-driving localization and mapping survey; direct full-text request was rate-limited (429). Use as a literature lead only until the article is inspectable; no detailed claims derived from inaccessible full text.",
    "https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/10261939": "Inspected indexed abstract/metadata for the 2023 IEEE vehicle-localization survey 2026-10-23. The abstract compares LiDAR/vision, IMU/GPS/radar/ultrasound and cooperative V2X and notes AI/compute trade-offs. Abstract-level taxonomy only; detailed claims remain open.",
    "https://nsl.cau.ac.kr/papers/ictc/ictc2024-choi-lidar-survey.pdf": "Located the authors' open PDF for the 2024 LiDAR localization survey after the IEEE record; it provides full-text access for method/map taxonomy inspection. It remains a survey, so primary studies are needed for comparative performance or route dependencies.",
    "https://aurora.tech/careers/f9fb3e3a-e5c1-418b-99c8-53e97b2f64f6": "Opened Aurora's current Senior Software Engineer, Localization posting 2026-10-23. It names high-rate multi-sensor vehicle pose estimation, safety/efficiency evaluation, C++/Python, state estimation, Kalman/nonlinear estimation, SLAM, LiDAR/IMU/radar/camera, spatial transforms and probability. Direct task evidence for this employer's specialist posting only.",
    "https://jobs.lever.co/waabi/ca67aa9c-d647-41d5-a45b-38d94304344a": "Opened Waabi's current Senior/Staff Localization Software Engineer posting 2026-10-23. It names IMU/LiDAR/radar/camera/GNSS/wheel sensors, factor graphs/Kalman, maps/semantic landmarks, large-scale and physical-track evaluation, and learned localization as a bonus. Employer-specific task evidence, not a universal requirement.",
    "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/kodiak/jobs/4412485009": "Opened Kodiak's current Staff Autonomy Software Engineer, Localization posting 2026-10-23. It describes localization/state estimation, inertial navigation and sensed odometry. Use only for the employer's specialist task context; do not infer universal software-developer duties.",
})

