    {"source_id":"D011-BOJ-LIQUIDITY-ADJUSTED-VAR-2000","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"Bank of Japan, Institute for Monetary and Economic Studies","title":"Research Toward the Practical Application of Liquidity Risk Evaluation Methods","url":"https://www.imes.boj.or.jp/research/abstracts/english/me18-2-4.html","source_family":"central-bank primary research","evidence_layer":"area_method_context","locator":"Yoshifumi Hisata and Yasuhiro Yamai, Monetary and Economic Studies 18(2), December 2000; official BOJ abstract page inspected 2026-10-26. Abstract describes liquidity-adjusted VaR (L-VaR), liquidation strategy with own market impact, and extensions to uncertain impact, multi-asset portfolios and nonlinear impact-volume relations; full-text PDF linked on the official page.","supports":"A market-liquidity risk method that combines position size, market impact, liquidation strategy and price risk; its output estimates loss while the position is optimally liquidated. Helps distinguish market-liquidity-adjusted loss estimation from a bank's funding cash-flow/gap and stress analysis.","claim_limit":"Historical research framework, not a current regulatory prescription or evidence of universal adoption. The abstract establishes the paper's described framework and extensions, not empirical superiority or a universal liquidity measure. Author views do not necessarily represent the BOJ/IMES.","search_status":"official publisher abstract inspected 2026-10-26; linked PDF identified","credibility_assessment":"Primary central-bank research publication with a clear author-view caveat; suitable for method description, not binding supervision or current-practice prevalence."},
    {"source_id":"D011-ECB-MARKET-FUNDING-LIQUIDITY-2023","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"European Central Bank","title":"Gauging the interplay between market liquidity and funding liquidity","url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/financial-stability-publications/fsr/special/html/ecb.fsrart202305_01~830184261b.en.html","source_family":"official central-bank financial-stability analysis","evidence_layer":"area_task_skill_activity","locator":"ECB Financial Stability Review special feature, May 2023, prepared by Nander de Vette, Benjamin Klaus, Simon Kördel and Andrzej Sowiński; full HTML inspected 2026-10-26. Defines market liquidity via ability to execute large transactions rapidly at low cost/limited impact and funding liquidity via borrowing/funding access; discusses indicators, measurement limits, margin/haircut and liquidity-spiral channels.","supports":"Provides an explicit conceptual and measurement distinction between market liquidity and bank funding liquidity, while documenting that they interact and can reinforce each other under stress. Market-liquidity indicators have multiple dimensions and no single indicator captures them all.","claim_limit":"Euro-area financial-stability analysis, not an individual firm liquidity rule or a universal estimator. Its composite indicators and empirical conclusions are sample/region-specific; do not collapse the distinct risk concepts merely because interaction is possible.","search_status":"full official ECB HTML inspected 2026-10-26","credibility_assessment":"Official central-bank analysis with inspectable methods and limitations; authoritative contextual evidence for the stated euro-area analysis, not binding regulation."}
