    {"source_id":"D011-IBM-QUANTUM-CREDIT-RISK-2021","domain_id":"D011","publisher":"IBM Research; originally published in IEEE Transactions on Computers","title":"Credit Risk Analysis Using Quantum Computers","url":"https://research.ibm.com/publications/credit-risk-analysis-using-quantum-computers","source_family":"research-institution summary of peer-reviewed quantum-credit-risk paper","evidence_layer":"area_method_context","locator":"Egger, Garcia Gutierrez, Cahue Mestre and Woerner, IEEE Transactions on Computers; IBM Research record dated 1 December 2021, opened 2026-10-24. Abstract covers credit economic capital (VaR minus expected loss) and qubit/circuit-depth/runtime scaling estimates under future fault-tolerant hardware assumptions.","supports":"A credit-risk-specific algorithm/resource pathway from a loss distribution and expected loss/VaR to economic-capital estimation; supports linking credit portfolio loss models to amplitude-estimation research.","claim_limit":"Only the IBM-hosted abstract was inspected. The claimed efficiency is a theoretical scaling/resource result conditional on future fault-tolerant hardware, not a current capital model or operational risk process.","credibility_assessment":"Research institution record of a peer-reviewed paper; authoritative for publication metadata and abstract summary, but detailed methods/results were not independently inspected here."},
