D011_METHOD_RELATIONSHIP_NOTES.append({
    "topic":"Backtest/model-selection diagnostics answer different multiple-testing questions and should be chosen by output, not treated as interchangeable",
    "finding":"First freeze and disclose the searched candidate universe, benchmark, loss/return measure, time window and trial ledger. White's Reality Check asks whether the best candidate in the searched family beats a benchmark, using a dependence-aware bootstrap; Hansen's SPA refines this benchmark test with studentization and sample-dependent null recentering, reducing sensitivity to weak alternatives. Romano–Wolf StepM returns which candidates beat a benchmark while controlling familywise error. Hansen–Lunde–Nason MCS returns a set of candidates not statistically distinguished from the best under a chosen loss and needs no benchmark. DSR adjusts a selected Sharpe ratio for the number/effective number of trials and non-normality. PBO/CSCV instead estimates how often an in-sample winner ranks poorly out of sample under combinatorial splits. Harvey–Liu–Zhu's higher significance hurdle addresses cross-sectional factor discovery; it is not a direct replacement for a strategy-level test. These methods are complements only when the research question and assumptions warrant them, not a mandatory bundle.",
    "source_ids":["D011-WHITE-REALITY-CHECK-2000","D011-HANSEN-SPA-2005","D011-ROMANO-WOLF-STEPM-2005","D011-HANSEN-LUNDE-NASON-MCS-2011","D011-BAILEY-LOPEZ-DSR-2014","D011-PBO-BACKTEST-OVERFIT-2017","D011-HARVEY-LIU-ZHU-FACTOR-MULTIPLE-TESTING-2016","D011-ARCH-MULTIPLE-COMPARISON-DOCS"],
    "prerequisite_context":"Requires a time-ordered, leakage-controlled backtest; a declared strategy/model universe and benchmark where applicable; a suitable loss or return statistic; and dependence-aware inference/bootstrap knowledge. Selection diagnostics do not repair look-ahead bias, survivorship bias, nonstationarity, an incomplete trial ledger, unrealistic trading costs or a poorly chosen benchmark. Outputs differ: one p-value for the best-vs-benchmark test, a superior-candidate set, a confidence set of top models, a deflated-Sharpe significance, or an overfit-probability estimate.",
    "prerequisite_source_ids":["D011-SCIKIT-TIME-SERIES-SPLIT","D011-PBO-BACKTEST-OVERFIT-2017","D011-WHITE-REALITY-CHECK-2000","D011-ARCH-MULTIPLE-COMPARISON-DOCS"],
    "claim_limit":"The primary procedures target different hypotheses, statistics, candidate universes and outputs; source abstracts and library docs do not prove one method universally dominates. The methods are candidates for systematic-investment research and require exact assumptions/implementation review; no technique becomes a canonical learning item or dependency solely from this note.",
    "role_task_relevance":[
        {"role_title":"quantitative researcher","relevance":"conditional strategy/model-selection research task","condition":"Use when the assignment searches and selects among many predictors, factors or strategies; direct research-task cards support research practice but not every test individually.","role_source_ids":["D011-JS-QUANT-RESEARCHER-2026","D011-TS-QUANT-RESEARCHER-ML-2025"]},
        {"role_title":"quantitative trader","relevance":"conditional systematic-strategy validation task","condition":"Use when a trading assignment develops or selects signals/parameters through repeated historical backtests; it does not imply all trading roles conduct research or use every diagnostic.","role_source_ids":["D011-JS-QUANT-TRADER-2026"]},
        {"role_title":"quantitative analyst","relevance":"conditional predictive/model validation task","condition":"Use when tasked with validating forecasts or models selected from multiple candidates; this is not inferred from title alone.","role_source_ids":["D011-ONET-QFA-2026"]}
    ]
})

D011_METHOD_RELATIONSHIP_NOTES.append({
    "topic":"Risk rules, regulatory capital measures and professional curricula answer different questions",
    "finding":"Basel MAR33 expected shortfall is a specific market-risk capital rule for banks using the internal models approach; CBN ICAAP/SREP guidance asks Nigerian banks to identify all material risks, quantify where suitable, assess internal capital and validate/stress-test the broader framework. Those are not interchangeable with a general practitioner’s VaR/ES estimate or a market-risk forecast. US Federal Reserve SR 26-2 is current model-risk guidance for its supervised-bank context, while SEC Nigeria adviser rules address client risk profiling, suitability and IPS records rather than institutional model risk. GARP FRM and CFA curricula organize learning coverage; they are credential syllabi, not statutes and not universal role prerequisites. The right contextual source depends on the employer, instrument, jurisdiction, portfolio/task and regulatory perimeter. A student-facing path should label these as conditional context choices and connect actual outputs (regulatory capital, internal capital/stress reports, model-validation evidence, or client suitability record) to the role task that consumes them.",
    "source_ids":["D011-BIS-MAR33-EXPECTED-SHORTFALL-2026","D011-CBN-ICAAP-SRP-2021","D011-CBN-BASEL-II-III-NIGERIA","D011-FED-SR26-2-2026","D011-SEC-NIGERIA-ROBO-ADVISORY-RULES","D011-GARP-FRM-CURRICULUM-2026","D011-CFA-2026-MEASURING-MANAGING-MARKET-RISK"],
    "claim_limit":"Basel is implemented through local law; the CBN guideline and 2020 Nigerian capital framework need current-status confirmation; SR 26-2 has a U.S. supervisory scope; SEC adviser rules are client-advisory context. FRM/CFA syllabi show published learning scope, not hiring or licensing requirements. No universal curriculum order is inferred.",
})

D011_METHOD_RELATIONSHIP_NOTES.append({
    "topic":"Initial-margin modelling consumes portfolio risk sensitivities, but it is not derivative pricing or market-risk capital",
    "finding":"ISDA SIMM v2.7+2412 uses sensitivities classified into risk-factor classes and aggregates delta, vega, curvature and other specified risk components to estimate initial margin for relevant non-centrally cleared derivatives. Under EU EMIR, firms may use the standardised grid or an authorised model; EBA centrally validates general aspects of the pro forma model while competent authorities authorize entity use and assess firm implementation. This is a downstream risk/collateral calculation, distinct from calculating a derivative's fair value or Basel market-risk capital. SIMM's currentness and regulatory context therefore belongs as a conditional risk-method/standards choice after derivative and portfolio risk foundations, not a universal prerequisite. Role evidence supports only broader conditional links: financial risk specialists may estimate/monitor risk and critique model outputs, while a derivatives quant analyst may build pricing and risk models. Those employer/occupational sources do not name SIMM; map the method to a role only when the assigned task actually covers uncleared-derivative margin, model implementation or validation.",
    "source_ids":["D011-ISDA-SIMM-METHODOLOGY-V2-7-2025","D011-EBA-CENTRAL-VALIDATION-ISDA-SIMM-2026","D011-BIS-UNCLEARED-MARGIN-REVIEW-2025","D011-BIS-MAR33-EXPECTED-SHORTFALL-2026"],
    "prerequisite_context":"Requires instrument/payoff and portfolio knowledge, sensitivity/risk-factor interpretation, aggregation and margin-framework scope. Pricing-model outputs may supply sensitivities, but an accurate pricing model alone does not establish correct SIMM mapping, licensing, governance or regulatory authorisation. Standardised-grid calculations and SIMM are alternative approaches only where permitted by the applicable margin framework; firm authorization and validation requirements are jurisdiction- and entity-specific.",
    "prerequisite_source_ids":["D011-CFA-CONTINGENT-CLAIMS-2026","D011-ISDA-SIMM-METHODOLOGY-V2-7-2025","D011-EBA-CENTRAL-VALIDATION-ISDA-SIMM-2026"],
    "claim_limit":"The detailed algorithm is proprietary/licensed and the public methodology is not independent validation. EBA statements are EU-specific, and entity/product thresholds must be checked in current law. BIS/BCBS corroborates implementation context, not global applicability. No role is asserted to use SIMM without task-specific evidence; this note supports later mapping review, not a graph edge or fixed learning dependency.",
    "role_task_relevance":[
        {"role_title":"financial risk specialist","relevance":"conditional portfolio risk-model monitoring/validation context","condition":"Relevant only when the assigned portfolio includes in-scope uncleared derivatives and the specialist's task includes margin model risk, monitoring or review. The cited evidence supports broader risk estimation, stress testing and model-output critique; it does not state that this role uses SIMM specifically.","role_source_ids":["D011-BLACKROCK-RQA-CAREER-2026"]},
        {"role_title":"quantitative analyst","relevance":"conditional derivatives risk-model implementation context","condition":"Relevant when the analyst develops or validates derivatives pricing/risk models and the specific product workflow includes regulatory initial margin. The cited Citi role supports derivatives pricing/risk model development but does not name SIMM or establish universal use.","role_source_ids":["D011-CITI-RATES-XVA-QUANT-ANALYST-2026"]}
    ]
})

D011_METHOD_RELATIONSHIP_NOTES.append({
    "topic":"Market-risk estimates branch by portfolio and loss-distribution assumptions; regulatory backtesting is a separate validation layer",
    "finding":"For market-risk VaR estimation, U.S. banking regulation explicitly recognizes variance-covariance, historical-simulation and Monte Carlo approaches; they are alternative estimation engines whose assumptions, nonlinear position treatment, risk-factor coverage, data window and computational cost must be checked against the portfolio. EVT, filtered historical simulation and conditional autoregressive VaR are further research families, but the reviews found in this pass were not fully accessible, so these remain leads for primary-paper confirmation rather than settled comparative recommendations. Regulatory output is a separate choice: the current Basel internal-model framework calculates market-risk capital with expected shortfall while MAR32 uses VaR backtesting and P&L attribution tests as eligibility/validation components. Neither a method's permitted use nor a backtest alone establishes adequate model quality. Validation also has a distinct lifecycle: conceptual soundness, alternative assumptions/benchmarking, out-of-sample/out-of-time tests, outcome analysis, ongoing monitoring and stress testing scaled to model materiality. Thus the path should distinguish risk-measure estimation, regulatory capital calculation and model validation, and connect only the branch required by the learner's institution, portfolio and assignment.",
    "source_ids":["D011-US-CFR-2026-217-203-MARKET-RISK-APPROACHES","D011-BIS-MAR32-BACKTESTING-PLA-CURRENT","D011-BIS-MAR33-EXPECTED-SHORTFALL-2026","D011-FED-SR26-2-2026","D011-RISK-VAR-METHODOLOGY-REVIEW-2013","D011-DYNAMIC-EVT-VAR-ES-REVIEW-2024"],
    "prerequisite_context":"Requires return/P&L and portfolio data, probability/distribution and dependence concepts, risk-factor mapping, valuation/sensitivity inputs for nonlinear positions, and a clearly defined horizon/confidence or tail objective. Backtesting then requires aligned forecasts and realized P&L/outcomes; regulatory capital tests additionally require the exact rule perimeter and prescribed portfolio/P&L definitions.",
    "prerequisite_source_ids":["D011-US-CFR-2026-217-203-MARKET-RISK-APPROACHES","D011-BIS-MAR32-BACKTESTING-PLA-CURRENT","D011-BIS-MAR33-EXPECTED-SHORTFALL-2026"],
    "claim_limit":"The CFR source applies to specified U.S. Board-regulated institutions under its market-risk rule; Basel standards depend on local adoption. The reviewed VaR papers differ in datasets, periods and evaluation, and their full texts were inaccessible in this search; no superiority ranking for EVT, FHS, CAViaR or any estimator is asserted. Broad role evidence does not show that a given role uses any named estimator or regulatory method.",
    "role_task_relevance":[
        {"role_title":"financial risk specialist","relevance":"conditional market-risk measurement and model monitoring","condition":"The role evidence supports statistical risk quantification, scenario analysis, risk-model development/monitoring and critique of model outputs. Specific estimator and bank regulatory capital tasks depend on the employer and portfolio; the cited evidence does not establish use of all three model families.","role_source_ids":["D011-ONET-13-2054.00","D011-BLACKROCK-RQA-CAREER-2026"]},
        {"role_title":"quantitative analyst","relevance":"conditional market-risk model development/validation","condition":"Relevant when a quantitative analyst's assignment builds or validates financial risk models; derivative-pricing roles may instead supply valuation/sensitivity inputs. The cited role examples are employer-specific and do not prove a universal VaR or Basel-capital task.","role_source_ids":["D011-ONET-QFA-2026","D011-CITI-RATES-XVA-QUANT-ANALYST-2026"]}
    ]
})

D011_METHOD_RELATIONSHIP_NOTES.append({
    "topic":"Derivative-pricing numerical methods form conditional branches; Monte Carlo, QMC, variance reduction and machine learning play different roles",
    "finding":"A learner should first specify the contract/payoff, model dynamics, market inputs and target output, then choose a numerical approach whose assumptions fit. Analytic/transform methods (including Carr-Madan FFT or COS) use characteristic-function structure and are natural for some European claims; trees and PDE discretizations expose time/space and early-exercise structure on tractable dimensions; simulation estimates expectations and can handle selected path-dependent or multifactor contracts. Longstaff-Schwartz is an optimal-stopping regression method that estimates continuation values, with weighted least squares proposed for heteroscedastic regressions in tested settings. MC variance-reduction methods (antithetic, control variates, stratification/importance sampling), low-discrepancy QMC and MLMC modify estimator variance/cost or path allocation; they do not change the economic pricing model. Brownian bridge and PCA are path-construction choices whose benefits depend on payoff and effective dimension; discontinuity-alignment can improve some QMC/Greek problems, but counterexamples rule out a universal ranking. Neural control variates are a research extension layered over an expectation estimator, not a beginner prerequisite or replacement for classical controls. Finally, price, Greeks, numerical uncertainty, convergence and exercise-policy outputs need separate validation because accurate prices can coexist with inaccurate sensitivities.",
    "source_ids":["D011-UCHICAGO-BLACK-SCHOLES-1973","D011-ELSEVIER-CRR-1979","D011-CUP-HULL-WHITE-EXPLICIT-FD-1990","D011-OUP-LONGSTAFF-SCHWARTZ-LSM-2001","D011-CARR-MADAN-FFT-1999","D011-FANG-OOSTERLEE-COS-2008","D011-BEHRENS-JUNIKE-SCHOUTENS-FOURIER-GREEKS-2025","D011-ACWORTH-BROADIE-GLASSERMAN-MCQMC-OPTIONS-1998","D011-PAPAGEORGIOU-QMC-BROWNIAN-BRIDGE-COUNTEREXAMPLE-2002","D011-WANG-TAN-QMC-DISCONTINUITY-ALIGNMENT-2013","D011-GILES-MLMC-OPTION-PRICING-2008","D011-GILES-MLMC-REFERENCE-CODE-2026","D011-FABOZZI-PALETTA-TUNARU-WLSMC-2017","D011-ELFILALI-LELONG-REGHAI-NEURAL-CONTROL-VARIATES-2021","D011-BROADIE-GLASSERMAN-MC-GREEKS-1996","D011-FOURNIE-MALLIAVIN-MC-GREEKS-1999","D011-GILES-GLASSERMAN-SMOKING-ADJOINTS-2005","D011-CAPRIOTTI-GILES-AAD-REVIEW-2024","D011-OPENGAMMA-AAD-CALIBRATION-IFT","D011-TONG-LIU-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING-GREEKS-2016","D011-CHAN-JOSHI-DISCONTINUOUS-GREEKS-2013","D011-SCOLERI-BIANCHETTI-KUCHERENKO-QMC-AAD-2021","D011-GILES-VIBRATO-MC-GREEKS-2009","D011-LAKSHTANOV-DISCONTINUOUS-GREEKS-PREPRINT-2026","D011-QUANTLIB-OPTION-ENGINE-COMPARISON"],
    "prerequisite_context":"The broad prerequisite chain is instrument/payoff and no-arbitrage pricing, probability and stochastic processes, then model-specific mathematics and numerical analysis (time/space discretization, Fourier transforms, regression, integration/error estimation). After learning the base Monte Carlo expectation estimator, students can select complementary variance-reduction/path-construction techniques; ML control variates require additional learning and should follow classical estimators and validation. These are conditional branches: a learner does not need every pricer for every contract.",
    "prerequisite_source_ids":["D011-CFA-CONTINGENT-CLAIMS-MODELS-2026","D011-SPRINGER-SHREVE-STOCHASTIC-CALCULUS-2004","D011-MIT-OCW-ANALYTICS-FINANCE-2010","D011-UWARSAW-COMPUTATIONAL-FINANCE-EXCEL-2026","D011-CARR-MADAN-FFT-1999","D011-OUP-LONGSTAFF-SCHWARTZ-LSM-2001"],
    "claim_limit":"The cited method papers study different contracts, processes, grids, dimensions and error criteria; several publisher records are abstract-only. This supports a conditional method map and evidence-backed connections, not a universal order, exhaustive method inventory, operational adoption claim or canonical graph dependency. Role relevance is conditional on assigned product and validation duties.",
    "role_task_relevance":[
        {"role_title":"quantitative analyst","relevance":"conditional pricing-model implementation and validation","condition":"Relevant when the analyst's assigned product requires valuation, calibration, Greeks or numerical model testing. Employer evidence supports derivatives pricing/risk-model work broadly, not use of every named scheme.","role_source_ids":["D011-CITI-RATES-XVA-QUANT-ANALYST-2026"]},
        {"role_title":"quantitative researcher","relevance":"conditional pricing-method research and benchmarking","condition":"Relevant when research work develops or compares valuation estimators/models; research title alone does not imply derivatives specialization or ML pricing.","role_source_ids":["D011-JS-QUANT-RESEARCHER-2026"]},
        {"role_title":"quantitative technology developer","relevance":"conditional numerical engine implementation and test infrastructure","condition":"Relevant where a developer implements a pricing library, numerical engine, calibration pipeline or validation tools; role evidence is not proof of ownership of model assumptions or product valuation decisions.","role_source_ids":["D011-CITI-QUANT-TECH-DEVELOPER-2026"]}
    ]
})

