    query_log.append({"query_id":"D011-QPRICE-QMC-COUNTEREXAMPLE-ML-EXTENSIONS-20261024","domain_id":"D011","area_id":"D011:quantitative-pricing-and-financial-engineering","query_family":"QMC path-construction and estimator extensions: ordinary MC versus QMC; Brownian bridge/PCA ordering; discontinuous-payoff and Greek estimation; neural-network effective-dimension reduction/control variates; counter-search for non-universal advantages","source_families":["primary peer-reviewed Management Science publisher abstract/full HTML","Journal of Complexity publisher abstract and author publication record","peer-reviewed journal abstract indexed by RePEc; full-text access explicitly limited"],"access_date":TODAY,"actual_queries":["Papageorgiou Brownian bridge no consistent advantage digital option QMC 2002 standard discretization publisher abstract","Wang Tan discontinuous payoff path generation QMC Greeks dimension reduction Management Science 2013 full abstract","neural network automatic control variates option pricing effective dimension 2021 De Gruyter abstract","Monte Carlo quasi Monte Carlo Brownian bridge PCA comparison does QMC always outperform option pricing counterexample"],"opened_pages_or_papers":["https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0885064X01906314","https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/mnsc.1120.1568","https://ideas.repec.org/a/bpj/mcmeap/v27y2021i2p91-104n7.html","https://www.cs.columbia.edu/~ap/html/body_publications.html"],"result":"Recorded both favorable and counterevidence: Acworth-Broadie-Glasserman's tested constructions often favor QMC/PCA; Papageorgiou's digital-option counterexample shows Brownian bridge can perform worse than standard path discretization; Wang-Tan report that path-generation design which aligns payoff discontinuities can materially improve QMC and Greeks in their experiments. A 2021 paper proposes neural-network control variates and effective-dimension reduction, but the indexed abstract is the inspected evidence and publisher full text is restricted. These findings indicate estimator/path construction must be chosen and benchmarked against the payoff and Greeks; no QMC or learned variance-reduction technique is universally superior."})
