    _risk_tool_current["claim_mappings"].append({
        "claim":"Risk-library and data-source choices depend on the risk output. Riskfolio-Lib 7.4 documents portfolio optimization using dispersion, downside/tail and drawdown measures, risk-parity/hierarchical allocation and risk contribution; it can support portfolio-level downside-aware construction, but does not replace instrument-level pricing or bank market, credit, counterparty or liquidity systems. For macro-financial covariates and scenario/backtest research, FRED/ALFRED provides named series metadata, observations and historical vintages; Federal Reserve Board research pages provide paper-specific datasets, definitions, frequencies and replication artifacts; ECB disseminated statistics are available through SDMX 2.1, while research microdata use separate eligibility/access procedures.",
        "locator":"Riskfolio-Lib 7.4 maintainer documentation (portfolio measures and optimization); PyPI project metadata; St. Louis Fed FRED API overview; Federal Reserve Board Economic Research Data catalogue, including its stated update frequencies; ECB official data access page, sections Data API and Access to microdata. Inspected 2026-10-26.",
        "source_ids":["D011-RISKFOLIO-LIB-DOCS-2026","D011-RISKFOLIO-LIB-PYPI-7-4-2026","D011-FRED-ALFRED-API-DATA-2026","D011-FED-ECON-RESEARCH-DATA-CATALOG-2026","D011-ECB-SDMX-DATA-ACCESS-2026"],
        "area_context":"These sources fit portfolio allocation/downside measurement and macro-financial research/scenario contexts. Frequency, vintages, definitions and access terms must fit the particular risk factor and holding period; high-frequency pricing, issuer/obligor data, transaction data, collateral/exposure data and production bank risk engines need separate sources.",
        "claim_limit":"Riskfolio-Lib documentation is maintainer capability evidence, not an independent benchmark or validation. The ECB dataset-catalogue endpoint returned 503 on the 2026-10-26 check, so this claim relies on its official data-access page for the API and microdata boundary, not a claim that specific catalogue datasets are currently available. Public aggregate or research series do not establish suitability, licensing or complete point-in-time history for a specific model.",
        "relationship_context":"Choose the measure/model first, then select an implementation that supports its assumptions and output; independently validate it. Select data by instrument, factor, frequency, vintage and access rights. A public macro series can enrich a scenario or historical research design but cannot stand in for the positions, market quotes, transaction-level credit or exposure data required for a production risk calculation."
    })
