    _risk_tech_current["evidence_ids"] = list(dict.fromkeys(_risk_tech_current.get("evidence_ids", []) + ["D011-FREY-MCNEIL-DEPENDENT-CREDIT-PORTFOLIOS-2002","D011-FED-INTERAGENCY-CCR-GUIDANCE-2011"]))
    _risk_tech_current["search_log_ids"] = list(dict.fromkeys(_risk_tech_current.get("search_log_ids", []) + ["D011-QRISK-CREDIT-DEPENDENCE-AND-ACCOUNTING-20261026"]))
    _risk_tech_current["claim_mappings"].append({
        "claim":"Credit-portfolio models encode default and dependence differently. Gordy's Fed comparison explains how CreditMetrics and CreditRisk+ differ in functional form, distributional assumptions and approximations; the open Fischer–Jakob chapter compares rating-migration/latent-asset CreditMetrics with actuarial factor-based CreditRisk+ and evaluates Gaussian, t, generalized-hyperbolic, Archimedean and vine-copula alternatives. A 2026 publisher record signals robust Bernoulli-mixture methods for parameter/copula ambiguity, but only abstract/indexed text was inspected.",
        "locator":"Gordy, FEDS 1999-28, abstract and full paper; Fischer and Jakob (2015), open chapter sections comparing model structures, dependence families and portfolio-loss results; Ansari (2026), Wiley abstract/indexed record only.",
        "source_ids":["D011-FED-CREDIT-MODEL-COMPARATIVE-ANATOMY-1999","D011-SPRINGER-COPULA-CREDIT-PORTFOLIO-MODELING-2015","D011-ANSARI-ROBUST-BERNOULLI-MIXTURE-CREDIT-2026","D011-FREY-MCNEIL-DEPENDENT-CREDIT-PORTFOLIOS-2002"],
        "area_context":"This is a portfolio-credit-loss modeling branch: obligor defaults, exposures, recovery/loss assumptions and dependence generate an aggregate loss distribution for tail-risk or economic-capital analysis. It is distinct from market-return VaR, IFRS 9 allowance estimation and counterparty exposure/CVA, even when data or risk components overlap.",
        "claim_limit":"The Fed paper is dated working research; the Springer chapter's numerical illustration uses a hypothetical portfolio, finite historical PD samples and deterministic LGD, and its comparisons do not establish a universal best copula. The Wiley 2026 source was not available as full text. Model choice, calibration and validation remain portfolio-, horizon- and purpose-specific.",
        "relationship_context":"CreditMetrics and CreditRisk+ are alternative model architectures; dependence families are alternatives within a portfolio model, not prerequisites to taking every branch. Exposure/default inputs and dependence assumptions precede loss-distribution estimation; sensitivity and backtesting/benchmarking outputs inform capital or portfolio decisions. The 2026 robust-model signal motivates uncertainty analysis but is not yet a selectable established method claim."
    })
